line 29, 35 extra: by-design spec §1.6 an `unknown` must be narrowed before it is used as a condition
line 191 type: by-design spec §1.6 `&&` keeps a type parameter in its falsy part, since a `T` can be falsy
line 366, 375 type: by-design spec §1.6 `==` is an alias for `===`, so `x == y` narrows `x` to the values it shares with `y`, where tsc keeps members `==` could coerce

line 86, 92, 119, 125, 173, 176 extra: by-design spec §1.6 `==` and `!=` against `null` or `undefined` are rejected, since they compare like `===` and would miss the other nullish value
line 90, 96 type: by-design spec §1.6 `!=` against `null` or `undefined` is rejected and checked as `!==`, so the equality branch contains only the tested nullish value
line 87, 93, 120, 126, 174, 177 type: by-design spec §1.6 `!=` against `null` or `undefined` is rejected and checked as `!==`, so the other nullish value stays
